Z||000000||Hippocrat||09-19-2001||02:01 AM||||Does anyone know if its possible to open the trunk with out keys? <BR>just saved a couple of SEs from the bone yard to restore them. The one does not have the keys. Not like the cars I'm used to .. before you just pop out the back seat remove the sound barrier and use the handy screwdriver. anyway .. any advise <P>If I have to pop the lock I have to .. <BR>would like to get around that for now though as the prev owner may find the keys but I got a lot of work to do. NOW.. <BR>thanx ||||reg||5
Z||000001||artherd||09-19-2001||03:52 AM||||call a locksmith  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Hippocrat:<BR><B>Does anyone know if its possible to open the trunk with out keys? <BR>just saved a couple of SEs from the bone yard to restore them. The one does not have the keys. Not like the cars I'm used to .. before you just pop out the back seat remove the sound barrier and use the handy screwdriver. anyway .. any advise <P>If I have to pop the lock I have to .. <BR>would like to get around that for now though as the prev owner may find the keys but I got a lot of work to do. NOW.. <BR>thanx </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||1
Z||000002||rogergarrison||09-19-2001||11:53 AM||||if it has power release, hook up a lighter plug to a battery, plug it into lighter socket and push it. If it dont have one, locksmith or drill a hole in the center of lock and use a slide hammer to yank out cylinder.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Philphine||09-19-2001||12:43 PM||||get all the people you know (and trust if thats an issue) with gm cars and try their keys. one of mine came with just an ignition key but one of my other door keys fits it (it also opens the drivers side of my chevy). one day when i've got time to kill i'm going to try all my keys in all the vehicles to see what opens what. might need to know one day.<P>------------------<BR>Phil T.<P>start where you are,<BR>use what you have,<BR>do what you can.||||reg||1
Z||000004||qwikgta||09-19-2001||08:57 PM||||I bought my 87 coupe at a auction, it came with no keys.  A locksmith was onsite making keys for $25.00.  He had a door/trunk key and ignition key made in less than 15 min.  I would call a locksmith b4 you force the lock<P>Rob||||reg||1
