Z||000007||Hippocrat||09-19-2001||09:50 PM||||Thanx for the responses.. sucked it up and yanked the cylinder.. installing power lock from the other Fiero. for future incidents.||||reg||14
Z||000008||Spektrum-87GT||09-19-2001||10:16 PM||||for future reference, if you dont mind going through the trouble of taking out the door lock cylinder, take it out like the haynes tells you to do(no pullers!), and take it down to a local locksmith, most will make a key for ~10 bucks(door key fits trunk lock). I've never done it with a fiero before... but i did do it with a cherokee, took me an hour from start to finish to take it out(frozen, rusted pieces everywhere) and i saved myself the 50 bucks a locksmith would have charged to come out.||||reg||1
